# Hillsbrad Foothills (30-32): the second visit to Tarren Mill (the Battle of Hillsbrad, the Elixir
# of Agony, Helcular's Revenge, the Dalaran internment camp and the Syndicate), with Bath'rah the
# Windwatcher in the Alterac Mountains for warriors and the Call of Water in Silverpine Forest for
# shamans, for a Horde duo.
#
# Built into the addon with:
#   python3 addon/tools/guide_build.py addon/guides/hillsbrad_foothills_30_32.guide --db data/forever.sqlite
#
# Research (November 2026): givers, objectives, prerequisites and the places of mobs and objects
# from the game data (data/forever.sqlite), checked against outof.games (Hillsbrad Foothills, area
# 267; Alterac Mountains, area 36) and the Wowhead WoW Forever comments; RestedXP's and Zygor's
# routes as a check. The quest list is section 12 of addon/guides/horde_1_40_allocation.md, plus
# Elixir of Agony (509, 513), moved here from Arathi Highlands (32-33) so the whole chain is done in
# one guide.
#
# Carried in (skipped by those who lack them): Battle of Hillsbrad (529), Souvenirs of Death (546)
#   and Dangerous! (567), from Tarren Mill on the first visit (Hillsbrad Foothills 22-24); for
#   warriors The Windwatcher (1791, Klannoc Macleod in the Barrens); for shamans Call of Water (63,
#   Islen Waterseer in the Barrens).
# Left to later guides: for warriors Cyclonian (1712) and Essence of the Exile (1714), taken from
#   Bath'rah and his cauldron here: the Bloodscalp Tusks come from Stranglethorn Vale (36-37) and
#   Alterac Mountains & Arathi Highlands (38-39) hands both in. For shamans Call of Water (96), the
#   Shard of Water for Islen Waterseer, handed in by Thousand Needles (33-34).
# Left out:
#   Regthar Deathgate (1361): a breadcrumb to Regthar Deathgate in the Barrens, which this guide
#     never visits (Nazgrel and Belgrom Rockmaul give it in Orgrimmar too).
#   Blood in the Streets (92434): it follows Dalaran Patrols (545), done in Alterac Mountains &
#     Arathi Highlands (38-39). Shrewd Negotiations (97287) follows Heart of Disruption (96984),
#     whose Arcane Mote is inside Dalaran, a dungeon.
#   Conquering Arathi Basin (8370) and Battle of Warsong Gulch (8426): they want battleground Marks
#     of Honor, won in PvP battlegrounds, not by questing.
# Bought, not farmed: Turtle Meat for cooks (the snapjaws hardly ever drop it in this game), in
#   Undercity at the start; the Troll's Blood elixir of Elixir of Agony (item 3388, called Lesser
#   Troll's Blood Elixir in this game; alchemists brew it, nothing drops it), in Undercity halfway.
#
# The route: Undercity and a flight to Tarren Mill; a loop north and west (Bath'rah for warriors,
# Valik in Sofera's Naze, the Foothill Caverns, the Lordamere Internment Camp, Hillsbrad Fields) and
# the hearthstone back; a second loop (Growless Cave, the Foothill Caverns again, the town hall of
# Hillsbrad Fields, Helcular's grave at Southshore, Nethander Stead); a flight to Undercity, where
# shamans fly on to the Sepulcher for the Call of Water and hearth back; a loop south-west (Azurelode
# Mine, the Torn Fin murlocs, the Daggerspine naga); a last loop to Dun Garok; the end in Tarren
# Mill, where Arathi Highlands (32-33) starts.

guide Hillsbrad Foothills (30-32)
faction horde
levels 30 32
carry 63 529 546 567 1112 1791
leave 96 1112 1712 1714
next Arathi Highlands (32-33)

# Undercity -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

map Durotar
note "From Kalimdor, take the zeppelin from the tower outside Orgrimmar to Tirisfal Glades, then walk into Undercity" at 50.8,13.4
map Undercity
ah 7321.1 npc 8672
tip Cooks only: Christoph Jeffcoat in Tarren Mill wants 10 Turtle Meat from each of you. Buy it here: in this game the snapjaws around Tarren Mill hardly ever drop it.
note "Optional: learn Cooking from Eunice Burch if you want the Soothing Turtle Bisque quest in Tarren Mill" npc 4552
tip Christoph Jeffcoat only offers it to those who know Cooking (Apprentice is enough); without it the guide skips that quest.
train 4593 260093 4582 4606 4566 4563
tip Hunters, shamans and druids have no trainer here: train at your next visit to Orgrimmar or Thunder Bluff.

