# North and west: Bath'rah, the Syndicate, the yetis, Dalaran's camp, Hillsbrad Fields ------------------

map Alterac Mountains
turnin 1791 only warrior
tip Bath'rah camps by the ruins on the east bank of the river, north-east of Tarren Mill.
accept 1712 only warrior
accept 1714 only warrior
tip Keep both: Bath'rah's cauldron takes the Exiles' charms for the Essence of the Exile, and the Bloodscalp Tusks of Cyclonian come from Stranglethorn Vale. Alterac Mountains & Arathi Highlands (38-39) finishes them.
accept 535
tip Henchman Valik lies wounded in Sofera's Naze, the Syndicate camp just north of Tarren Mill in the Alterac Mountains. Walk past the patrols to him; he is not hostile. He only talks to those on Krusk's Infiltration.
do 535
tip No stout? The Drunken Footpad who wanders the camp nearly always drops one.
turnin 535
tip Hand it in before you loot any Syndicate Missive: Valik won't take the stout from someone who already carries one. His missive completes Infiltration. He may turn on you after the hand-in: kill him, and if one of you has not handed in yet, wait for his respawn.
do 533
tip Done with Valik's missive. Otherwise the Syndicate Footpads and Thieves of the camp drop it, about one in three.

map Hillsbrad Foothills
do 552
tip The yetis' cave (the Foothill Caverns, on Darrow Hill) opens in the hills west of Tarren Mill; any yeti in or just outside it can drop the rod. It is a very rare drop: players report anything from 20 to over 250 kills. In a group it drops for both of you at once. Skinners do well here; everyone else: give it a while, then right-click to skip Helcular's Revenge.

map Alterac Mountains
do 556 bg
tip The Lordamere Internment Camp is the walled compound on a hill south of Dalaran, left of the road. The Dalaran mages around it drop the tokens, the Shield Guards most often. A Shield Guard's red shield hurts whoever hits it in melee: stop meleeing while it is up (spells and ranged attacks can carry on). The elementals nearby see you from far away and drop nothing: go around them. Players find the tokens slow in this game, with few mages and many hunters: if it drags on, right-click to skip Stone Tokens (Bracers of Binding, its follow-up in a later guide, then skips itself).
do 544
tip Ricter, Alina, Dermot and Kegan Darkmar are passive undead prisoners (they don't attack first): each carries one Bloodstone piece. The first three are in and around the walled camp; Kegan Darkmar (35) is upstairs in the two-storey house west of it, with guards and a caster who polymorphs: pull the guards first.
do 93680
tip The Warden's Footlocker is not inside the walled camp: walk past its west wall to the two-storey house beyond it, go into the second room on the ground floor, and the chest stands at the back by the stairs, near Warden Belamoore. Each of you opens it.
do 556

map Hillsbrad Foothills
do 546 bg mobs 2267 2266 2360 2268 2387 2265 2264 2269 2503 2270
tip Every human of Hillsbrad can drop a skull, but players get only about one in ten in this game and each of you needs 30: kill every human you pass in the fields, the town and the mine. The Battle of Hillsbrad brings you back here twice more.
do 529
tip The smithy stands just north of the road through Hillsbrad Fields: Blacksmith Verringtan and his apprentices work there, and the Shipment of Iron is inside the workshop. The apprentices are slow to respawn and seem to need room: clear the other mobs around the smithy if none come back. Already done on the first visit? Nothing to do.
do 567.1
tip Clerk Horrace Whitesteed is inside the town hall, the walled white house in the west of the town, among the Councilmen. Kill him now; you come back here for the Magistrate later.
do 567.2
tip Citizen Wilkes walks the road between the town hall and the smithy. These named humans take about half an hour to respawn: if someone got there first, do the rest and check again.
do 567.4
tip Farmer Kalaba works among the trees of the orchard by the road, on the east side of the fields.
hearth npc 2388

