# Silverpine Forest: the Call of Water (shamans) ------------------------------------------------------

fly "The Sepulcher, Silverpine Forest" npc 4551 only shaman
map Silverpine Forest
goto "Climb into the hills behind the Sepulcher's inn and cross them west to the shrine of Everfount" at 41.8,41.2 r 15 only shaman
tip A tall tree stands against the rocks behind the inn: jump up the rocks beside it, then head west over the ridge and drop down to the coast (the falls hurt a little). The shrine is a big standing stone by a ring-shaped pool.
do 63 only shaman
tip Stand next to the standing stone and drink the Water Sapta: water elementals appear around the pool. Only one can be attacked, the corrupt one near the middle (level 22): kill it for the bracers. If someone killed it just before you, it is back within about 5 minutes. Something went wrong? Tiev Mordune, sitting behind the stone, helps those who bring him another Sapta.
turnin 63 only shaman
tip Put the bracers and the Remaining Drops of Purest Water on the Brazier of Everfount.
accept 100 only shaman
turnin 100 only shaman
tip The Minor Manifestation of Water appears on the islet in the middle of the pool a few seconds later. It wanders off if you wait too long, and comes back after a few minutes.
accept 96 only shaman
tip Keep the Shard of Water: Thousand Needles (33-34) takes it to Islen Waterseer.
hearth npc 2388 only shaman
tip There is no short way back to the Sepulcher: your hearthstone takes you to Tarren Mill. Not ready yet? Walk north around the mountains and back to the Sepulcher, and fly to Tarren Mill.

# Azurelode Mine, the Torn Fin murlocs, the Daggerspine naga --------------------------------------

map Hillsbrad Foothills
do 539
tip Azurelode Mine is just south of Hillsbrad Fields; the sentries outside call each other for help, the miners inside come one at a time (they run when hurt). Foreman Bonds stands on a raised platform deep inside (the entrance is on its south-west side; take the lower way in, then the first fork right). Below 20% he calls two dwarves: burst him down, or stun him as he gets low.
do 567.3
tip Miner Hackett is in the north-east nook of the mine, where you can jump down to a lower level.
do 546 at 29.8,55.5 mobs 2269 2503 2270 2266 2267
tip Still short of skulls? The miners seem to drop them more often; the Syndicate mages of Durnholde Keep, south-east of Tarren Mill across the river, are another good source. Or right-click to skip Souvenirs of Death.
do 515.3 at 28.0,71.0
tip The Torn Fin murlocs on the beach just south of Azurelode Mine drop the eyes more often than the big crowd south-west of Southshore. Still only about one in seven, and each of you needs five: pull the loners, groups of murlocs run for help.
do 515.2
tip The Daggerspine naga line the river mouth between Southshore and Nethander Stead, and the coast further south-east. About one in four drops a scale, and Sirens hit hard: fight them one at a time. Alliance players farm here too.

